Day 13
-------

this keyword -> always represent the class/object

2 types of variables
1)class/instance variables
2)local variables

NOTE : in java there is no global variable concept

static keyword
--------------
static is a keyword in Java. It means the member (variable or method) belongs to the class instead of individual objects.

Static keyword can be applied for variables and methods.

static variables->A static variable is shared by all objects of the class.
static methods->A static method belongs to the class, not to an object.

Non - static 
------------
A non-static member belongs to an object, not to the class.

This means:

Every object has its own copy of non-static variables.
Non-static methods can access both static and non-static members.
You must create an object to access non-static members.


non-static variables->A non-static variable is declared without the static keyword.
non-static methods->A non-static method belongs to an object. You must create an object before calling it.

1) static methods can access static variables and methods without creating any object 
2) static methods can access non-static stuff through object
3) non-static methods can access everything directly
4) if we access static variable or methods in another main method we have to specify the classname with the variable or method name
